• What it fixes: /spawn -o "out/a b.md" do x now saves to out/a b.md and runs the task do x, with single or double quotes. An unquoted path works as before, and so does a bare -o with nothing after it (it becomes task text). Quotes inside the task text are handled exactly as before.
• Shared quote reader: -o and --system now read their values through one helper in the new file src/commands_spawn_args.rs. The old inline --system quote handling was removed, so there's no third copy.
